            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Robert C. HILLIARD (Petitioners), according to Robert C. HILLIARD (Petitioners), sergio Hernandez, a 15\u2011year\u2011old Mexican citizen, was standing unarmed on Mexican soil when he was shot and killed by a U.S. Border Patrol agent who was standing inside the United States."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Robert C. HILLIARD (Petitioners)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Robert C. HILLIARD (Petitioners), according to Robert C. HILLIARD (Petitioners), the petitioners argue that because all of the officer\u2019s conduct occurred inside the United States, the Fourth Amendment\u2019s restrictions on deadly force apply."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Ortega",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a0133059bf61-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Ortega, the respondent argues that the Fourth Amendment does not apply to a cross\u2011border shooting that occurs on Mexican soil."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a0133059bf610ecb7f9a0bb0f8bd3c4b037df6516ccc61db821cd8cd84570715",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a0133059bf61-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, the Court is asked to decide whether a Bivens action for Fourth Amendment violations is available when a U.S. officer shoots a foreign national on foreign soil from a position inside the United States."
      }
    ],
